[Audio:allophones:AL2 Allophones]
The #FACT(sp0256,SP0256-AL2) set, as written by #R$0166. These
are recordings of a real chip, not a simulated core. The samples
derive from CPCWiki's AL2 WAV set (via ExtremeElectronics), which
CPCWiki notes has some allophone lengths wrong. Bit 6
(high intonation) is not applied here; the
#R$0447 entries play it where the ROM sets that bit.

The AL2 set is 59 allophones plus 5 pauses, each analysed with
LPC. Datasheet pause lengths are PA1-PA5 = 10 / 30 / 50 / 100 /
200 ms (datasheet nominal; CPCWiki computes 6.4 / 25.6 / 44.8 /
96.0 / 198.4 ms from the ROM); the datasheet also gives a sample
word for each ID (for example OY "boy", AY "sky"). The
#FACT(sstring,s$) interpreter never maps a character or name to
three IDs: #N$00 (PA1), #N$02 (PA3) and #N$36 (DH2). The s$
tables give 61 of the 64 IDs; with the key dictionary (which uses
PA1) the ROM gives 62, never PA3 or DH2; the manual names only 0
and 54 as unimplemented, so it misses PA3. See the AL2
datasheet linked from #LINK(Credits)(Credits).

